From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: ID3D11Fence, CreateFence, OpenSharedFence, Signal, Wait (3628)

d3d11: ID3D11Fence (CreateFence, OpenSharedFence, Signal, Wait)

The fence value lives in a shared memory section, so a fence made with
D3D11_FENCE_FLAG_SHARED hands out a handle (CreateSharedHandle) another device or
process opens with OpenSharedFence. The value only goes up (Signal with a lower
value leaves it), SetEventOnCompletion signals the event once the value is
reached (at once if it already is), and the immediate context's Signal flushes the
queued commands before it raises the value; Wait blocks the caller until the value
is reached. Browser/Office-facing (d3d11): run their checks at integration.
---
